From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:46:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: connac: keep a VHT station's short GI across tx
 statuses

A tx status reports the rate without its guard interval. For HT the
short GI flag is carried over from the station's rate, as the station
poll last read it from the WTBL, and for HE the GI is. For VHT the flags
were set to RATE_INFO_FLAGS_VHT_MCS alone, so every status of a VHT
station turned its rate to long GI until the next poll: the rate
reported for it flipped between the two, and the airtime mac80211
estimates from it for AQL was too long in between.

mt76_connac_test_txs_modes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt76_connac_mac.c       | 7 +++++++
 tests/connac-mac-test.c | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt76_connac_mac.c b/mt76_connac_mac.c
index d0d0f2da..cdecfd39 100644
--- a/mt76_connac_mac.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mac.c
@@ -731,6 +731,13 @@ bool mt76_connac2_mac_fill_txs(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
 			return false;
 
 		rate.flags = RATE_INFO_FLAGS_VHT_MCS;
+		/*
+		 * The status has no guard interval: as for HT and HE, it stays
+		 * what the station poll last read, or every status would turn
+		 * a VHT station's rate to long GI until the next poll.
+		 */
+		if (wcid->rate.flags & RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI)
+			rate.flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
 		break;
 	case MT_PHY_TYPE_HE_SU:
 	case MT_PHY_TYPE_HE_EXT_SU:
diff --git a/tests/connac-mac-test.c b/tests/connac-mac-test.c
index 854c55e5..1453b25a 100644
--- a/tests/connac-mac-test.c
+++ b/tests/connac-mac-test.c
@@ -1269,6 +1269,11 @@ static void mt76_connac_test_txs_modes(struct kunit *test)
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, wcid->rate.bw, RATE_INFO_BW_160);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, wcid->stats.tx_bw[3], 1);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, wcid->stats.tx_nss[2], 1);
+	/* its short GI, once the station poll has read it, stays as for HT */
+	wcid->rate.flags |= RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI;
+	KUNIT_ASSERT_TRUE(test, mt76_connac2_mac_fill_txs(dev, wcid, txs));
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, wcid->rate.flags,
+			RATE_INFO_FLAGS_VHT_MCS | RATE_INFO_FLAGS_SHORT_GI);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, mt76_connac2_mac_fill_txs(dev, wcid,
 		(__le32[8]){ mt76_connac_test_txs(MT_PHY_TYPE_VHT, 10, 1, 0,
 						  0) }));
